-- title:
--   Lifting edge-chart coordinates along a nilpotent thickening
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $K$, let $\pi \in \mathcal O$ be irreducible with finite residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ of cardinality $q$, and let $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ be the matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$. Let $B$ and $B'$ be commutative $\mathcal O$-algebras and $\varphi \colon B' \to B$ a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map whose kernel is a nilpotent ideal, and assume the image of $\pi$ in $B'$ is nilpotent. Let $d$ be a Deligne datum over $B$ (a family of $B$-submodules $d.\mathrm{line}\,M \subseteq B \otimes_{\mathcal O} M$, one for each full lattice $M$ in $K^2$, with invertible quotients, compatible with inclusions and with the homothety action, and nondegenerate at every prime of $B$) such that $d$ satisfies `InEdgeChart` for the pair of lattices $g\cdot\mathcal O^2$, $\mathcal O^2$, i.e. $d$ is edge-nondegenerate at that pair at every prime ideal of $B$. Let $x \colon$ `chartERing 𝒪 π q` $\to B$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map — `chartERing 𝒪 π q` being the localisation of the edge-chart ring away from `edgeQuot.discr 𝒪 π q`, with distinguished elements $\xi$ and $\eta$ — presenting the lines of $d$ in normal form: $d.\mathrm{line}(\mathcal O^2)$ is the $B$-span of $x(\xi) \otimes e_0 + 1 \otimes e_1$, and $d.\mathrm{line}(g\cdot\mathcal O^2)$ is the image under the base-changed action isomorphism $B \otimes \mathcal O^2 \cong B \otimes (g\cdot\mathcal O^2)$ of the $B$-span of $1 \otimes e_0 + x(\eta) \otimes e_1$. Finally let $d'$ be a Deligne datum over $B'$ whose base change along $\varphi$ is $d$, i.e. $d.\mathrm{line}\,M$ is the line generated by the image of $d'.\mathrm{line}\,M$ for every full lattice $M$. Then there is an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $x' \colon$ `chartERing 𝒪 π q` $\to B'$ with $\varphi \circ x' = x$ which presents the lines of $d'$ in the same normal form, with $x'(\xi)$ and $x'(\eta)$ in place of $x(\xi)$ and $x(\eta)$.
--
--   This is the deformation-theoretic lifting step for points of the formal upper half plane in the standard edge chart: a lift $d'$ of a Deligne datum along a surjection with nilpotent kernel automatically lifts the edge-chart coordinates $\xi,\eta$ of its chart point. It is used in the construction of quadruples attached to Drinfeld data, where a lifted datum must be matched with a lifted chart morphism.
